    <briefdescription>
<para>Concept satisfied by the character types. </para>
    </briefdescription>
    <detaileddescription>
<para>The <computeroutput>character</computeroutput> concept is satisfied when the type, ignoring the cv-qualifiers, is one of <computeroutput>char</computeroutput>, <computeroutput>wchar_t</computeroutput>, <computeroutput>char8_t</computeroutput>, <computeroutput>char16_t</computeroutput>, or <computeroutput>char32_t</computeroutput>. The comparators compare the arrays and the pointers of these types as strings (see <computeroutput>basic_c_string</computeroutput>); <computeroutput>signed char</computeroutput> and <computeroutput>unsigned char</computeroutput> are not characters, but bytes.</para>
